<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Autonomous Republic of Northern Epirus</h1><p class="st-meta">1914 CE – 1914 CE · capital Gjirokaster</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived republic declared in 1914 by the Greek population of southern Albania, which won autonomy before the First World War overtook it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a> of 1912-1913 left Greek troops in southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a>, a region with a large Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> population that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> called Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>. The Protocol of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-florence">Florence</a> in December 1913 assigned it to the new state of Albania. Rejecting this, local leaders proclaimed an autonomous republic at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjirokaster">Gjirokaster</a> in February 1914, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgios-christakis-zografos">Georgios Christakis-Zografos</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The provisional government raised its own armed units, issued stamps and fought Albanian gendarmerie for control of the region. In May 1914 the Protocol of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corcyra">Corfu</a>, accepted by the Albanian government and the great powers, gave the region extensive autonomy within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a>, with Greek-language schools and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> religious rights.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Protocol of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corcyra">Corfu</a> was never fully put into effect. With the outbreak of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and Albania's collapse, the Greek army occupied the region in October 1914, ending the republic. The area was returned to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> after the war.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/autonomous-republic-of-northern-epirus.jpg" alt="Autonomous Republic of Northern Epirus" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Philly boy92 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Autonomous_Republic_of_Northern_Epirus.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1914 CE – 1914 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gjirokaster</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Georgios Christakis-Zografos</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Northern Epirus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1914&amp;focus=autonomous-republic-of-northern-epirus" aria-label="Autonomous Republic of Northern Epirus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5176 744 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Autonomous Republic of Northern Epirus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5496 1000L5475 960M5496 1000L5591 1068"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5475 960h0M5591 1068h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5496 1000h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5496 1000h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gjirokaster. <a href="/atlas?year=1914&amp;focus=autonomous-republic-of-northern-epirus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
